\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Timeline. Pipeline phases on the x-axis; the four gates' allow decisions as marks along the top; the per-phase behavioral divergence below, with its clean-baseline band. The compromise curve (red) spikes at the tester (AUC 1.00) and rises at the deployer (AUC 0.87). The benign controls (blue) drift as far at each measured phase, a benign override at the tester (0.97) and a benign atypical target at the deployer (0.84), so the compromise and benign-anomaly points coincide and no threshold on the divergence separates malice from a benign departure. That coincidence is the paper's central result.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:timeline}{{3}{8}{}{figure.3}{}}
